{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914484546,"sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_6ecd45fc7866470497899b27","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_parcels.py"},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_parcels.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import unittest\n2: from datetime import date, datetime\n3: from decimal import Decimal\n4: \n5: from parcels.delivery import add_working_days, delivery_date\n6: from parcels.packing import parcel_weights\n7: from parcels.quote import CannotShip, shipping_cost\n8: \n9: \n10: class ParcelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n11:     def test_heavy_orders_are_split_evenly(self):\n12:         self.assertEqual(parcel_weights(Decimal(\"70\")), [Decimal(\"23.334\")] * 3)\n13: \n14:     def test_free_shipping_and_destinations(self):\n15:         self.assertEqual(shipping_cost(Decimal(\"80\"), Decimal(\"2\"), \"de\"), Decimal(\"0.00\"))\n16:         with self.assertRaises(CannotShip):\n17:             shipping_cost(Decimal(\"10\"), Decimal(\"1\"), \"US\")\n18: \n19:     def test_weekends_are_skipped(self):\n20:         self.assertEqual(add_working_days(date(2026, 3, 6), 1), date(2026, 3, 9))\n21:         self.assertEqual(delivery_date(datetime(2026, 3, 5, 16, 0), \"NL\"), date(2026, 3, 10))\n22: \n23: \n24: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n25:     unittest.main()\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import unittest\nfrom datetime import date, datetime\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nfrom parcels.delivery import add_working_days, delivery_date\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import CannotShip, shipping_cost\n\n\nclass ParcelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_heavy_orders_are_split_evenly(self):\n        self.assertEqual(parcel_weights(Decimal(\"70\")), [Decimal(\"23.334\")] * 3)\n\n    def test_free_shipping_and_destinations(self):\n        self.assertEqual(shipping_cost(Decimal(\"80\"), Decimal(\"2\"), \"de\"), Decimal(\"0.00\"))\n        with self.assertRaises(CannotShip):\n            shipping_cost(Decimal(\"10\"), Decimal(\"1\"), \"US\")\n\n    def test_weekends_are_skipped(self):\n        self.assertEqual(add_working_days(date(2026, 3, 6), 1), date(2026, 3, 9))","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_parcels.py","text":"import unittest\nfrom datetime import date, datetime\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nfrom parcels.delivery import add_working_days, delivery_date\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import CannotShip, shipping_cost\n\n\nclass ParcelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_heavy_orders_are_split_evenly(self):\n        self.assertEqual(parcel_weights(Decimal(\"70\")), [Decimal(\"23.334\")] * 3)\n\n    def test_free_shipping_and_destinations(self):\n        self.assertEqual(shipping_cost(Decimal(\"80\"), Decimal(\"2\"), \"de\"), Decimal(\"0.00\"))\n        with self.assertRaises(CannotShip):\n            shipping_cost(Decimal(\"10\"), Decimal(\"1\"), \"US\")\n\n    def test_weekends_are_skipped(self):\n        self.assertEqual(add_working_days(date(2026, 3, 6), 1), date(2026, 3, 9))\n        self.assertEqual(delivery_date(datetime(2026, 3, 5, 16, 0), \"NL\"), date(2026, 3, 10))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":25,"totalLines":25,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/test_parcels.py","time":{"start":1794914484489,"end":1794914484520}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me read the tests to understand expected behaviors, especially around heavy orders.\n\nNote Q2: \"What happens to an order that is heavier than a single parcel may be?\" - The `parcel_weights` splits into multiple parcels of equal weight, each at most MAX_PARCEL_KG. But there's a subtlety: with ROUND_CEILING quantization, the each weight could exceed MAX_PARCEL_KG? Let's check: total=70, MAX=31.5, count=ceil(70/31.5)=3, each = 70/3 = 23.3333... -> 23.334. Fine.\n\nBut what about total_kg = 31.6? count = ceil(31.6/31.5) = 2, each = 15.8. Fine.\n\nHmm, but what about the rounding: total = 63.1, count = ceil(63.1/31.5) = ceil(2.003) = 3, each = 21.0333 -> 21.034. Fine.\n\nActually is there a case where each exceeds MAX_PARCEL_KG? count = ceil(total/MAX), so each = total/count <= total/ceil(total/MAX). Since ceil(total/MAX) >= total/MAX, each <= MAX. So never exceeds. Good.\n\nSo Q2: heavy order gets split into multiple parcels, each priced separately (shipping cost is the sum of parcel prices). Also note there's no upper limit on total weight — no error. Let's check tests.\n\nAlso note that the round-up quantization means the total packed weight can slightly exceed the original total (e.g., 3 * 23.334 = 70.002), and the price uses math.ceil(weight_kg) — for a parcel of 23.334 kg, ceil = 24 started kg. Interesting.\n\nLet me read the tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e93d80f3001g8kUtMsb4Dj8b7","sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","messageID":"msg_1e93d7970001wYFWwdd6zuMtO5"}}
