{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914490412,"sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_7e781a19e78a4729850c27f2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 --version && python3 -c \"\nfrom datetime import datetime, date\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom parcels.delivery import delivery_date, add_working_days\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost\nimport parcels.settings as s\nprint('carrier', s.CARRIER, 'free_from', s.FREE_SHIPPING_FROM, 'max', s.MAX_PARCEL_KG, 'handling', s.HANDLING_DAYS)\nfor c in ['NL','DE','BE','FR','LU']:\n    d = delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,20,17,0), c)\n    print(c, d, d.strftime('%A'))\nprint('friday17 start->', (datetime(2026,11,20,17,0).date()))\nprint('weights 70:', parcel_weights(Decimal('70')))\nprint('weights 31.6:', parcel_weights(Decimal('31.6')))\nprint('weights 31.5:', parcel_weights(Decimal('31.5')))\nprint('weights 32:', parcel_weights(Decimal('32')))\nprint('cost 70kg DE:', shipping_cost(Decimal('10'), Decimal('70'), 'DE'))\nprint('cost 59.99 NL 2kg:', shipping_cost(Decimal('59.99'), Decimal('2'), 'NL'))\nprint('cost 60 NL 2kg:', shipping_cost(Decimal('60'), Decimal('2'), 'NL'))\n\"\n"},"output":"Python 3.10.15\ncarrier postnl free_from 60.00 max 31.5 handling 1\nNL 2026-11-24 Tuesday\nDE 2026-11-25 Wednesday\nBE 2026-11-25 Wednesday\nFR 2026-11-27 Friday\nLU 2026-11-25 Wednesday\nfriday17 start-> 2026-11-20\nweights 70: [Decimal('23.334'), Decimal('23.334'), Decimal('23.334')]\nweights 31.6: [Decimal('15.800'), Decimal('15.800')]\nweights 31.5: [Decimal('31.500')]\nweights 32: [Decimal('16.000'), Decimal('16.000')]\ncost 70kg DE: 66.45\ncost 59.99 NL 2kg: 5.00\ncost 60 NL 2kg: 0.00\n","metadata":{"output":"Python 3.10.15\ncarrier postnl free_from 60.00 max 31.5 handling 1\nNL 2026-11-24 Tuesday\nDE 2026-11-25 Wednesday\nBE 2026-11-25 Wednesday\nFR 2026-11-27 Friday\nLU 2026-11-25 Wednesday\nfriday17 start-> 2026-11-20\nweights 70: [Decimal('23.334'), Decimal('23.334'), Decimal('23.334')]\nweights 31.6: [Decimal('15.800'), Decimal('15.800')]\nweights 31.5: [Decimal('31.500')]\nweights 32: [Decimal('16.000'), Decimal('16.000')]\ncost 70kg DE: 66.45\ncost 59.99 NL 2kg: 5.00\ncost 60 NL 2kg: 0.00\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 --version && python3 -c \"\nfrom datetime import datetime, date\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom parcels.delivery import delivery_date, add_working_days\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost\nimport parcels.settings as s\nprint('carrier', s.CARRIER, 'free_from', s.FREE_SHIPPING_FROM, 'max', s.MAX_PARCEL_KG, 'handling', s.HANDLING_DAYS)\nfor c in ['NL','DE','BE','FR','LU']:\n    d = delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,20,17,0), c)\n    print(c, d, d.strftime('%A'))\nprint('friday17 start->', (datetime(2026,11,20,17,0).date()))\nprint('weights 70:', parcel_weights(Decimal('70')))\nprint('weights 31.6:', parcel_weights(Decimal('31.6')))\nprint('weights 31.5:', parcel_weights(Decimal('31.5')))\nprint('weights 32:', parcel_weights(Decimal('32')))\nprint('cost 70kg DE:', shipping_cost(Decimal('10'), Decimal('70'), 'DE'))\nprint('cost 59.99 NL 2kg:', shipping_cost(Decimal('59.99'), Decimal('2'), 'NL'))\nprint('cost 60 NL 2kg:', shipping_cost(Decimal('60'), Decimal('2'), 'NL'))\n\"\n","time":{"start":1794914490280,"end":1794914490411}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me verify Q4 precisely: order placed Friday at 17:00.\n\n- ordered.hour = 17 >= CUTOFF_HOUR (15) → start = Friday + 1 day = Saturday.\n- transit = TRANSIT_DAYS.get(country.upper(), DEFAULT_TRANSIT_DAYS). For NL → 1; DE → 2; others → 4.\n- add_working_days(Saturday, HANDLING_DAYS + transit) = add_working_days(Sat, 1 + transit).\n\nadd_working_days: current = Sat; days = 1+transit. Loop: current = Sun (weekday 6, not <5, no decrement), current = Mon (weekday 0, decrement → days = transit), then continue: current = Tue (decrement → transit-1)... So it adds transit working days starting from Monday.\n\nWait — let's carefully count. days = 1 + transit (e.g., NL: 2).\n- current = Sat → +1 = Sun (weekday=6) → not counted, days still 2.\n- +1 = Mon (weekday=0) → counted, days = 1.\n- +1 = Tue (weekday=1) → counted, days = 0. Stop.\n\nResult: Tuesday. So for NL, Friday 17:00 order → Tuesday.\n\nFor DE (transit 2): days = 3:\n- Sun skip, Mon → days=2, Tue → days=1, Wed → days=0 → Wednesday.\n\nFor default (transit 4): days = 5: Mon,Tue,Wed,Thu,Fri → Friday of the following week.\n\nNote that start on Saturday doesn't skip the weekend in a special way — the weekend is just skipped as non-working days. Important: the cutoff pushes to Saturday, then the weekend days are skipped since they're not working days. So effectively start becomes Monday.\n\nNote holidays are NOT accounted for — docstring says \"holidays are not\" (parcels/delivery.py:15).\n\nLet me verify with actual code execution.\n\nAlso for Q1: free shipping from 60.00 EUR, changeable via env var PARCELS_FREE_FROM (parcels/settings.py:15). Note: value is in euros after discounts, and only applies inside the EU (well, the check `order_value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM` happens after the EU check, so it applies to EU destinations only; non-EU raises CannotShip). Comparison uses `>=` so exactly 60.00 is free.\n\nNote: there's a subtlety — the free shipping threshold check happens before packing, so free shipping covers multi-parcel orders too.\n\nQ3: default carrier is \"postnl\" via `os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_CARRIER\", \"postnl\")` (parcels/settings.py:10), lowercase; allowed values dhl, ups, postnl (settings.py:8); invalid → RuntimeError at import (settings.py:11-12). Another carrier is chosen by setting the PARCELS_CARRIER env var before importing parcels. Note settings are read at import time (module docstring line 1) so changing env var at runtime after import has no effect — needs to be set before process start / import.\n\nQ2: An order heavier than MAX_PARCEL_KG (31.5 kg) is split into multiple parcels, as few as possible, all of equal weight, each rounded up to the gram (packing.py:11-22). Each parcel is priced separately and the shipping cost is the sum (quote.py:33). There's no error/limit for very heavy orders — no upper bound on total weight; also note that the sum of parcel weights can slightly exceed the original weight due to ROUND_CEILING.\n\nLet me run the code to verify the numbers.\n\nLet me check for git history — maybe there's something about intended behavior, e.g., a missing feature. But the question says \"Do not change any code.\" I just need to answer.\n\nLet me verify by running python.\n\nAlso check whether there's an env var for holidays. There isn't. Let me double check by grepping for \"holiday\".","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e93d97860015k8ZXqOCd3MikI","sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","messageID":"msg_1e93d81c1001G5LVBqds76PD0p"}}
