{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914545484,"sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_d76aff6eda404963a398fdeb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom parcels.delivery import delivery_date\nprint('Mon 16 Nov 14:00 NL ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,16,14,0),'NL').strftime('%a %d %b'))\nprint('Mon 16 Nov 17:00 NL ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,16,17,0),'NL').strftime('%a %d %b'))\nprint('Fri 20 Nov 14:00 NL ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,20,14,0),'NL').strftime('%a %d %b'))\nprint('Fri 20 Nov 17:00 NL ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,20,17,0),'NL').strftime('%a %d %b'))\nprint('Fri 20 Nov 17:00 DE ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,20,17,0),'DE').strftime('%a %d %b'))\nprint('Fri 20 Nov 17:00 FR ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,20,17,0),'FR').strftime('%a %d %b'))\n\""},"output":"Mon 16 Nov 14:00 NL -> Wed 18 Nov\nMon 16 Nov 17:00 NL -> Thu 19 Nov\nFri 20 Nov 14:00 NL -> Tue 24 Nov\nFri 20 Nov 17:00 NL -> Tue 24 Nov\nFri 20 Nov 17:00 DE -> Wed 25 Nov\nFri 20 Nov 17:00 FR -> Fri 27 Nov\n","metadata":{"output":"Mon 16 Nov 14:00 NL -> Wed 18 Nov\nMon 16 Nov 17:00 NL -> Thu 19 Nov\nFri 20 Nov 14:00 NL -> Tue 24 Nov\nFri 20 Nov 17:00 NL -> Tue 24 Nov\nFri 20 Nov 17:00 DE -> Wed 25 Nov\nFri 20 Nov 17:00 FR -> Fri 27 Nov\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 -c \"\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom parcels.delivery import delivery_date\nprint('Mon 16 Nov 14:00 NL ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,16,14,0),'NL').strftime('%a %d %b'))\nprint('Mon 16 Nov 17:00 NL ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,16,17,0),'NL').strftime('%a %d %b'))\nprint('Fri 20 Nov 14:00 NL ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,20,14,0),'NL').strftime('%a %d %b'))\nprint('Fri 20 Nov 17:00 NL ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,20,17,0),'NL').strftime('%a %d %b'))\nprint('Fri 20 Nov 17:00 DE ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,20,17,0),'DE').strftime('%a %d %b'))\nprint('Fri 20 Nov 17:00 FR ->', delivery_date(datetime(2026,11,20,17,0),'FR').strftime('%a %d %b'))\n\"","time":{"start":1794914545395,"end":1794914545482}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me verify the Friday 17:00 case in detail. Order placed Friday at 17:00 → cutoff hour 15 → start = Saturday. Then add_working_days(Saturday, HANDLING_DAYS + transit).\n\nFor NL: transit=1, HANDLING=1 → 2 working days from Saturday. Working days counted from Saturday: current += 1 day each iteration. Start Saturday → next day Sunday (weekday 6, not counted) → Monday (counted, 1) → Tuesday (counted, 2) → Tuesday 2026-11-24. Matches output.\n\nNote interesting subtlety: because start rolls to Saturday (a weekend), and the weekend days are skipped anyway, the Friday-17:00 order for NL gets the same date as a Friday-14:59 order. Actually Friday 14:59: start = Friday, add_working_days(Friday, 2) → Sat(skip) Sun(skip) Mon(1) Tue(2) → Tuesday too. Yes same.\n\nAlso worth noting: the `add_working_days` treats the start day itself as not counted — it always increments first. So for Saturday start, Sat→Sun(skip)→Mon(1). The weekend skip is double-counted but that's fine.\n\nAlso note: no holiday support — the docstring explicitly says holidays are not skipped. So public holidays are NOT accounted for; only weekends.\n\nAlso worth mentioning the country-dependence of transit days: NL=1, BE/DE/LU=2, everything else=4.\n\nLet me double check the heavy order question (Q2). An order heavier than MAX_PARCEL_KG (31.5 kg) is split into multiple parcels, each of equal weight, rounded up to the gram, and each parcel is priced separately (so shipping cost is multiplied). There's no error/limit for very heavy orders — 200 kg → 7 parcels. Note: MAX_PARCEL_KG is a constant not configurable via env.\n\nAlso note the rounding: each parcel weight is rounded up to the gram, so total packed weight can slightly exceed the actual weight (70 kg → 70.002 kg), and price uses math.ceil(kg) per parcel, so 23.334 kg bills as 24 kg.\n\nQ1: Free shipping from 60.00 EUR, orders at or above the value (after discounts) ship free. Changed via env var PARCELS_FREE_FROM. Note: it's read at import time (settings module docstring line 1) so changing it requires restarting the process. Also note the free-shipping check happens before packing, so heavy orders over threshold are also free.\n\nWait — also important: the free shipping threshold check happens after the EU check. So it only applies to EU destinations.\n\nLet me also note the currency is euros, and `Decimal(os.environ.get(...))` will raise InvalidOperation if the env var isn't a valid decimal.\n\nQ3: default carrier postnl (settings.py:10), configurable via PARCELS_CARRIER env var, validated against CARRIERS tuple at import time with RuntimeError. Case-insensitive via .lower(). Tariffs in carriers.py:16-20.\n\nNote also: the carrier selection is at import time, and it's the module-level constant read once. Changing env var at runtime after import has no effect.\n\nLet me verify the timing claim: settings.py says \"Settings read from the environment once, at import.\" Yes.\n\nAlso note: changing carrier changes prices but NOT transit days — TRANSIT_DAYS is keyed by country only (delivery.py:9). That's a worthwhile observation for the newcomer.\n\nLet me also double check the delivery date for Friday 17:00 more carefully and per-country, and check what happens if the start lands on Saturday. Let me also verify: for a Friday 17:00 order, the date is the same as a Friday pre-cutoff order for NL and DE, but not for 4-day transit countries? Let's check: Friday 14:59, DE: start = Friday, add_working_days(Fri, 1+2=3) → Sat skip, Sun skip, Mon(1), Tue(2), Wed(3) → Wed 25. Friday 17:00, DE: start = Saturday → Sun skip, Mon(1), Tue(2), Wed(3) → Wed 25. Same. Interesting — because the weekend absorbs the extra day.\n\nActually for a country with 4-day transit: Friday 17:00 → Sat start → Mon(1) Tue(2) Wed(3) Thu(4) Fri(5) = 1+4=5 working days → Fri 27. Friday 14:59 → Fri start → Sat skip Sun skip Mon(1)...Fri(5) → Fri 27. Same.\n\nSo for a Friday order, the cutoff rollover into Saturday makes no difference because weekends are skipped either way. Good insight.\n\nBut if the order is placed Friday at 17:00 and the start rolls to Saturday — the weekend skip is inherent. Note also: what about a Monday 17:00 order → start Tuesday, so a day later than Monday 14:00. Let's verify: Monday 17:00 NL: start=Tue, add 2 working days → Wed(1) Thu(2) = Thursday. Monday 14:00 NL: start=Mon → Tue(1) Wed(2) = Wednesday. So yes, day-of-week matters except Friday.\n\nLet me verify with the actual code for Monday.\n\nAlso for Q4 I should mention holidays are NOT accounted for (delivery.py:15 docstring) — a known gap.\n\nLet me compute a concrete worked example with an actual date. Let me use a specific upcoming Friday relative to today (2026-11-17 is a Tuesday per env). The next Friday is 2026-11-20. Good.\n\nLet me verify Monday comparison.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e93e6ed40017p2YHoLNr9ADu4","sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","messageID":"msg_1e93e52e7001doyh3pLq0RJAqF"}}
