{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914553195,"sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_62ce8fc790934a9ca54ce0b9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"MAX_PARCEL_KG\\|HANDLING_DAYS\\|FREE_SHIPPING_FROM\\|CARRIER\" --include=\"*.py\" . | grep -v \"\\.git/\""},"output":"./parcels/delivery.py:7:from parcels.settings import HANDLING_DAYS\n./parcels/delivery.py:30:    return add_working_days(start, HANDLING_DAYS + transit)\n./parcels/quote.py:10:from parcels.settings import CARRIER, FREE_SHIPPING_FROM\n./parcels/quote.py:18:    tariff = TARIFFS[CARRIER]\n./parcels/quote.py:31:    if order_value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM:\n./parcels/packing.py:8:from parcels.settings import MAX_PARCEL_KG\n./parcels/packing.py:15:    ``MAX_PARCEL_KG``: 70 kg becomes three parcels of 23.334 kg (rounded up to the gram).\n./parcels/packing.py:20:    count = max(1, math.ceil(total_kg / MAX_PARCEL_KG))\n./parcels/settings.py:8:CARRIERS = (\"dhl\", \"ups\", \"postnl\")\n./parcels/settings.py:10:CARRIER = os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_CARRIER\", \"postnl\").lower()\n./parcels/settings.py:11:if CARRIER not in CARRIERS:\n./parcels/settings.py:12:    raise RuntimeError(f\"PARCELS_CARRIER must be one of {', '.join(CARRIERS)}, not {CARRIER!r}\")\n./parcels/settings.py:15:FREE_SHIPPING_FROM = Decimal(os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_FREE_FROM\", \"60.00\"))\n./parcels/settings.py:17:MAX_PARCEL_KG = Decimal(\"31.5\")\n./parcels/settings.py:18:HANDLING_DAYS = 1\n","metadata":{"output":"./parcels/delivery.py:7:from parcels.settings import HANDLING_DAYS\n./parcels/delivery.py:30:    return add_working_days(start, HANDLING_DAYS + transit)\n./parcels/quote.py:10:from parcels.settings import CARRIER, FREE_SHIPPING_FROM\n./parcels/quote.py:18:    tariff = TARIFFS[CARRIER]\n./parcels/quote.py:31:    if order_value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM:\n./parcels/packing.py:8:from parcels.settings import MAX_PARCEL_KG\n./parcels/packing.py:15:    ``MAX_PARCEL_KG``: 70 kg becomes three parcels of 23.334 kg (rounded up to the gram).\n./parcels/packing.py:20:    count = max(1, math.ceil(total_kg / MAX_PARCEL_KG))\n./parcels/settings.py:8:CARRIERS = (\"dhl\", \"ups\", \"postnl\")\n./parcels/settings.py:10:CARRIER = os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_CARRIER\", \"postnl\").lower()\n./parcels/settings.py:11:if CARRIER not in CARRIERS:\n./parcels/settings.py:12:    raise RuntimeError(f\"PARCELS_CARRIER must be one of {', '.join(CARRIERS)}, not {CARRIER!r}\")\n./parcels/settings.py:15:FREE_SHIPPING_FROM = Decimal(os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_FREE_FROM\", \"60.00\"))\n./parcels/settings.py:17:MAX_PARCEL_KG = Decimal(\"31.5\")\n./parcels/settings.py:18:HANDLING_DAYS = 1\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn \"MAX_PARCEL_KG\\|HANDLING_DAYS\\|FREE_SHIPPING_FROM\\|CARRIER\" --include=\"*.py\" . | grep -v \"\\.git/\"","time":{"start":1794914553167,"end":1794914553194}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting: Friday 17:00 for NL gives Tuesday 24 Nov — same as Friday 14:00, because cutoff pushes start to Saturday, and Saturday/Sunday are skipped, so effectively Monday + 2 working days = Tuesday. Wait, let's trace: start = Saturday 21 Nov. add_working_days(Sat, HANDLING_DAYS + transit = 1+1 = 2). current=Sat; loop: current += 1 day → Sun (weekday 6, not counted), → Mon (counted, days=1), → Tue (counted, days=0) → Tuesday 24. Yes.\n\nInteresting note: for NL, Friday 17:00 = Tuesday 24, same as Friday 14:00 → start Friday, +2 working days: Sat skip, Sun skip, Mon (1), Tue (2) → Tuesday 24. Same result coincidentally.\n\nAlso note: cutoff is hour-based only — 15:00 exactly counts as after cutoff; minute is ignored.\n\nAlso note that \"cutoff\" rolls to next day even if next day is Saturday — but then weekends are skipped anyway.\n\nHolidays: explicitly NOT accounted for (delivery.py:15 docstring). So public holidays count as normal working days.\n\nAlso worth noting the transit days are country-based, not carrier-based — so switching carrier changes price but not delivery date. That's an important observation for Q3/Q4.\n\nNow Q2: heavier than a single parcel — split into multiple parcels of equal weight, as few as possible, each ≤ MAX_PARCEL_KG (31.5 kg), rounded up to the gram. The rounding-up means the sum of parcel weights can slightly exceed the original total (70 kg → 3 × 23.334 = 70.002 kg). Each parcel is charged separately, and each parcel's price uses ceil of the parcel weight in kg (started kilograms) — 23.334 kg rounds up to 24 billed kg. So total shipping for 70 kg to DE = 3 × 22.15 = 66.45.\n\nAlso note MAX_PARCEL_KG is not configurable via env var — only carrier and free-shipping threshold are.\n\nLet me double check parcel price rounding for various cases, and whether an order of e.g. 0 weight raises. Also check the case where total_kg <= 0 raises ValueError.\n\nAlso check: does parcel_weights ever produce a parcel above MAX_PARCEL_KG after rounding up to the gram? E.g. total = 31.5 → count=1, each = 31.500 exactly. total = 63.0 → count = ceil(63/31.5) = 2, each = 31.5. total=63.1 → count=3, each=21.034. Rounding up to the gram could exceed MAX_PARCEL_KG if MAX_PARCEL_KG weren't a whole number of grams — 31.5 is exactly 31.500, so each ≤ 31.5 exactly since each ≤ total/count ≤ 31.5 and rounding up to gram... hmm, each ≤ 31.5; if each is 31.49999 → rounds up to 31.500, still ≤ 31.5. But if each = 31.5 exactly then quantize keeps 31.500. Actually could rounding push above 31.5? each ≤ MAX_PARCEL_KG = 31.5 exactly since total/count ≤ 31.5 mathematically; quantization rounds up to nearest 0.001 which is ≤ 31.500 as long as value ≤ 31.5. So safe. Fine, no need to claim a bug there.\n\nBut there IS a subtle thing: the billed price uses math.ceil(weight_kg) of the parcel weight → 23.334 bills as 24 kg.\n\nLet me verify a couple of Q1 details: free shipping threshold is \"at or above\" 60.00 EUR, after discounts (per the docstring/comment), inside EU. Actually the comment says \"ship for free inside the EU\" — but the code path: country must be in EU (else CannotShip), then if order_value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM → 0. So free shipping applies to all EU destinations. Change via env var PARCELS_FREE_FROM, read at import time (settings docstring line 1) — so it must be set before the process starts/imports parcels. Also note that the value is used in `Decimal` comparison; parsing errors raise InvalidOperation at import.\n\nAlso note that the threshold applies only to order_value after discounts (caller's responsibility).\n\nLet me verify the README / __main__ CLI: `python -m parcels VALUE WEIGHT_KG COUNTRY`. Nothing else configures the threshold.\n\nLet me also check git history for hints — only one commit \"fixture\".\n\nOne more check for Q3: the carrier is chosen by PARCELS_CARRIER env var, one of dhl/ups/postnl, lowercased, invalid raises RuntimeError at import. And TARIFFS in carriers.py:16-20. Also worth noting: the delivery/transit times are NOT carrier-dependent (delivery.py:9-10), so switching carrier changes price only.\n\nLet me also confirm the exact behavior for Q2 regarding \"what happens\" — no error is raised for heavy orders; they're split, not rejected. There's no upper limit on total weight — 200 kg → 7 parcels. Let me check there's no max total weight anywhere. Confirmed via grep for MAX_PARCEL_KG usage.\n\nLet me grep MAX_PARCEL_KG usages.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e93e8d44001WlPMqNU68S44Vt","sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","messageID":"msg_1e93e704b001E15F4dHKquNNrY"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914555974,"sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_555a55f3ddac49538a463f61","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost\n# edge cases\nfor t in ['0','-1','0.001','31.5','31.51','63','63.01']:\n    try:\n        print(t, parcel_weights(Decimal(t)))\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(t, 'ERR', e)\nprint('free shipping applies regardless of weight:', shipping_cost(Decimal('80'), Decimal('200'), 'DE'))\n\""},"output":"0 ERR an order weighs something\n-1 ERR an order weighs something\n0.001 [Decimal('0.001')]\n31.5 [Decimal('31.500')]\n31.51 [Decimal('15.755'), Decimal('15.755')]\n63 [Decimal('31.500'), Decimal('31.500')]\n63.01 [Decimal('21.004'), Decimal('21.004'), Decimal('21.004')]\nfree shipping applies regardless of weight: 0.00\n","metadata":{"output":"0 ERR an order weighs something\n-1 ERR an order weighs something\n0.001 [Decimal('0.001')]\n31.5 [Decimal('31.500')]\n31.51 [Decimal('15.755'), Decimal('15.755')]\n63 [Decimal('31.500'), Decimal('31.500')]\n63.01 [Decimal('21.004'), Decimal('21.004'), Decimal('21.004')]\nfree shipping applies regardless of weight: 0.00\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 -c \"\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost\n# edge cases\nfor t in ['0','-1','0.001','31.5','31.51','63','63.01']:\n    try:\n        print(t, parcel_weights(Decimal(t)))\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(t, 'ERR', e)\nprint('free shipping applies regardless of weight:', shipping_cost(Decimal('80'), Decimal('200'), 'DE'))\n\"","time":{"start":1794914555902,"end":1794914555971}},"id":"prt_1e93e974a00134bAqXhi9LW9CN","sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","messageID":"msg_1e93e704b001E15F4dHKquNNrY"}}
