{"type":"text","timestamp":1794914578605,"sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","part":{"id":"prt_1e93eed0b001q24yhUEoCZO4DL","messageID":"msg_1e93eea6b001vCA4Pro3FwPJjw","sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeOBXo75aiTjuQ8B","type":"text","text":"Created `ANSWERS.md` (no code changed; tests still pass). Summary:\n\n1. **Free shipping from €60.00** (`parcels/settings.py:15`), applied as `order_value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM` (`parcels/quote.py:31-32`). Change via `PARCELS_FREE_FROM` env var — but settings are read once at import (`parcels/settings.py:1`), so it must be set before process start.\n\n2. **Heavy orders are split**, not rejected: `ceil(total_kg / 31.5)` parcels of equal weight rounded up to the gram (`parcels/packing.py:20-21`, `parcels/settings.py:17`), each priced separately and summed (`parcels/quote.py:33`). 70 kg → 3 × 23.334 kg.\n\n3. **Default carrier is `postnl`** (`parcels/settings.py:10`); override with `PARCELS_CARRIER` (dhl/ups/postnl, invalid → `RuntimeError` at import, `parcels/settings.py:11-12`). It only affects pricing, not transit times.\n\n4. **Friday 17:00** is past the 15:00 cutoff (`parcels/delivery.py:11,27-28`) → handled from Saturday; weekends are skipped (`parcels/delivery.py:20`) but **public holidays are not** (`parcels/delivery.py:15`) — no holiday calendar exists. Result for Fri 20 Nov 2026: NL → Tue 24 Nov, DE/BE/LU → Wed 25 Nov, other EU → Fri 27 Nov.","time":{"start":1794914577675,"end":1794914578601}}}
